    {
      "id": "span-style-font-size-2-5rem-letter-spacing-0-003em-8-nbsp-how-to-approach-these-problems-span",
      "title": "<span style=\"font-size: 2.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">8.&nbsp;How to Approach These Problems</span>",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 1: Identify the structure</strong><br>Check if the problem is a tree, a DAG, or a general graph with cycles.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 2: Define your subproblem</strong><br>Decide what&nbsp;<code>dp[node]</code>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<code>dp[node][state]</code>&nbsp;represents.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 3: Find the recurrence</strong><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Tree → combine results from children</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">DAG → take best from all predecessors</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Cycles → use transitions with extra state (like bitmask)</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 4: Identify base cases</strong><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Tree → leaf nodes</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Graph → nodes with no incoming edges</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 5: Decide traversal order</strong><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Tree → post-order DFS (children first)</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">DAG → topological order</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Cycles → process states in increasing mask size</span>"
          ]
        },
        {
